Task: Add agentSundries and otherIncome to RentalScheduleInput (Phase 2, Tier 1)

WHAT CHANGED
  lib/tax/rental-schedule.ts
    RentalScheduleInput  + otherIncome?, agentSundries?  (both optional)
    RentalSchedule       + otherIncome, totalIncome
    netResult is now totalIncome − totalDeductions
  tests/lib/tax/rental-schedule.test.ts — 7 tests added

THE CORE WHY
Two ATO lines the schedule could not express:

- Agent bank and admin charges are not commission. Routing them to the existing
  `sundry` line rather than `agent_fees` is what leaves the commission figure
  directly comparable to the management_fee_pct estimate it replaces — mix them
  and you can no longer tell whether a discrepancy is a missing letting fee or a
  bank charge.
- Tenant reimbursements are assessable income on a line SEPARATE from gross
  rent. Folding them into gross rent would break the tenancy accrual
  cross-check in rental-income.ts, which compares against weekly_rent x weeks.

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Both inputs OPTIONAL with a zero default, so every existing caller and test is
  unaffected. Confirmed: all pre-existing rental-schedule and portfolio tests
  pass unchanged.
- Agent sundries are ADDED to the sundry line rather than given their own. The
  ATO reports one sundry line whatever the charges were for; a second line would
  not map onto the form.
- otherIncome uses apportionIncome, not apportionDeduction. Ownership applies,
  but availability and private use reduce deductions only and must never reduce
  an assessable amount. There is a test at 50% ownership.
- totalIncome is exposed rather than left for callers to add up, so the pack and
  the report cannot disagree about what net result was measured against.
- An excluded primary residence returns zero for both, tested — it has no rental
  schedule at all.

